    "answer": {
      "short": "$8,\\ 3,\\ 7,\\ 7,\\ 7,\\ 7$, in any order in the six empty cards.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Number of 8s}&=8\\times\\frac14\\\\\\text{Number of 8s}&=2\\\\\\text{Number of 7s}&=8\\times\\frac12\\\\\\text{Number of 7s}&=4\\end{align*}$$\nOne 8 is already shown, so the missing cards include one 8 and four 7s. With the supplied 6, the final number must give a range of 5. It is 3 because $8-3=5$. The alternative, 11, is ruled out because no number exceeds 10.\nThe six missing numbers are $8,3,7,7,7,7$, in any order.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
